  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lot 17A: Multi-Donor Trust Fund Supported Health Sector Transformation Project South Sudan - Unity State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Country faces significant challenges that adversely affect its human capital with one of the lowest Human Capital Index (HCI)8 scores at 0.31.
Cultural norms and a preference for larger families dampen the demand for reproductive and maternal health services. 
Acute malnutrition remains a major public health emergency in South Sudan.
The country grapples with frequent disease outbreaks exacerbated by conflict, persistent seasonal flooding,

Build and sustain experience of &#xA0;Coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) Emergency Response and Health System Preparedness Project (CERHSPP) and the health pooled fund (HPF) with a focus on improving service availability including to refugees and host communities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To expand access to a basic package of health and nutrition services, improve health sector stewardship, and strengthen the health system.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women of reproductive age and children under five
Host communities and refugees will 
Programme will offer all-inclusive services, and all patients are served from all communities, all gender and other social construct including Person with disabilities</narrative>
  </description>
